What prompt engineering is — simply put, it's the skill of giving AI clear, structured instructions so you get useful results instead of vague ones.
The 4-part formula every good prompt follows: Role → Task → Context → Format. Think of it like briefing a smart colleague — the more context you give, the better the output.
4 real examples you can use right now as a data analyst:

Cleaning messy data with Python/pandas
Generating charts from raw data
Extracting business insights automatically
Writing SQL queries in plain English

6 career skills it unlocks: faster exploratory data analysis, dashboard building, executive reporting, code debugging, statistical modelling, and communicating to non-technical stakeholders.
